  "dormant_paths": [
    {
      "detail": "The Groq and Gemini transports are exercised against a fake urlopen that pins the URL, headers, body shape, retry behaviour and every error branch. No socket has been opened to either service from this repository.",
      "kind": "live network path",
      "location": "providers.py :: _post_json, against a real endpoint"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Credential resolution and client construction are driven with a fake boto3 session. No live Bedrock call is made in CI or in this run.",
      "kind": "live network path",
      "location": "providers.py :: _bedrock_client, live session"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The final else in the dispatch cannot be reached because ModelSpec rejects an unknown provider at construction. It is kept so that adding a provider to PROVIDERS without adding a transport fails loudly instead of silently.",
      "kind": "defensive, unreachable",
      "location": "providers.py :: complete, unsupported-provider fallback"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The LLM render of a whole seed is human-triggered for cost control, so no seed in this run was rendered by a model. The orchestration is not dormant: a test drives render_seed in llm mode with only the converse call stubbed and asserts every artifact, and separate tests cover the fidelity retry loop and the exhausted-retry outcome. What has never executed here is the HTTP call.",
      "kind": "live network path",
      "location": "scenarios/renderer.py :: render_seed(deterministic=False), against live Bedrock"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The oracle audit is human-triggered. ask_oracle is tested against a capturing client; run_audit's verdict logic is tested through classify(), which the calibration suite drives directly.",
      "kind": "live network path",
      "location": "verify/answerability.py :: run_audit, against a live model"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Only the us. inference profile is used in practice because that is what config.yaml sets; the eu. and apac. prefixes are accepted but never taken.",
      "kind": "unreachable with the shipped config",
      "location": "providers.py :: BEDROCK_PROFILE_PREFIXES, eu. and apac."
    },
    {
      "detail": "A supersession graph can only become cyclic via a fact with two successors, and build_successor_map rejects that first. The double-supersession guard is tested; this one cannot be reached through any public shape and is kept as a backstop.",
      "kind": "defensive, provably unreachable",
      "location": "universe/generator.py :: supersession_chains, cycle guard"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The rate ladder has twelve rungs and no chain uses more than three, so the exhaustion raise never fires on seeds 42, 43 or 44.",
      "kind": "guard never fired",
      "location": "universe/generator.py :: bump_cpm, ladder-exhausted raise"
    },
    {
      "detail": "44 advertiser roots against at most 12 advertisers, and 18 agency roots against at most 7 agencies. The raise protects a future increase in entity counts.",
      "kind": "guard never fired",
      "location": "universe/generator.py :: _distinct_names, wordlist-exhausted raise"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Both raise if an (entity, attribute) pair has two active facts. The duplicate_active_facts quota now makes that impossible at generation time, so the runtime raise is redundant protection. It fired once during development, which is why the quota exists.",
      "kind": "guard never fired",
      "location": "universe/generator.py :: current_value / UniverseIndex.active_at, multi-active raise"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The generator produces facts on (order_system, system), (email_received, counterparty), (email_sent, user) and (call_note, user). The other five rows -- (order_system, user), (email_sent, system), (email_received, system), (email_received, user) and (call_note, counterparty) -- are derived correctly and tested directly, but no fact in any of the three universes carries them.",
      "kind": "table entry with no generated fact",
      "location": "universe/schema.py :: TRUST_TABLE, five of nine rows"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The schema allows an 'agency' entity but the generator records agency relationships as advertiser attributes (agency_of_record), so no fact has entity == 'agency' and the label branch is never taken.",
      "kind": "branch with no data",
      "location": "questions/instantiate.py :: UniverseIndex.label, agency entity branch"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Fabricated order-line ids use the 9xxx block and real ones never reach it, so the collision check never skips.",
      "kind": "guard never fired",
      "location": "questions/instantiate.py :: build_abstention_false_premise, fake-id collision guard"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The 'no progress' break covers a universe with fewer candidates than the target total. All three seeds have surplus, so allocation always reaches its target and the break is not used.",
      "kind": "branch never taken",
      "location": "questions/instantiate.py :: allocate, starvation break"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Sentence splitting declines to split after a single capital letter (an initial such as 'J. Whitfield'). The generator never produces initials, so only the abbreviation-word half of the guard runs against the corpus. Both halves are covered by the matching self-tests.",
      "kind": "branch with no data",
      "location": "verify/matching.py :: _is_abbreviation_boundary, single-initial branch"
    },
    {
      "detail": "It raises if the resolved region is empty, but settings.aws_region raises a ConfigError naming aws.region before it can return an empty value. The ConfigError path is tested; this guard cannot be reached.",
      "kind": "defensive, unreachable",
      "location": "providers.py :: _bedrock_client, empty-region guard"
    },
    {
      "detail": "The per-scenario failure printout is exercised by the CLI failure test but never by a clean run, because the deterministic corpus has no fidelity failures.",
      "kind": "branch reached only on failure",
      "location": "verify/fidelity.py :: main, failure detail printing"
    }
  ],
